> integrate x^2 from 0 to 1 numerically qmc points 1024 replicates 2 seed 0
∫ x^2 numerically, x from 0 to 1
  quasi-Monte Carlo (an estimate, not a proof): 0.3335085049, standard error 0.00024
    2 randomised replicates of 1024 Sobol points in 1 dimension (Joe-Kuo direction numbers, a random digital shift each; seed 0)
    the error is estimated from the 2 replicates' spread: +-0.0031 at 95% if their means are normal (t = 12.706), which nothing proves
